dation or destruction  also we have to force ourselves to the  same panelists and our countries in  Europe that are now in the VMP  population the cost of environmental  degradation and destruction is there a  way these can be the worldwide global  scale also be a development in the  future thank you thank you I clearly  made a mistake by not asking you to to  come up here that was a very eloquent  statement thank you so much well the the  question had several parts to it one was  the distinction between growing forests  and conserving forests and surely  existing forests should be conserved not  so much because they take carbon dioxide  out of the atmosphere but because they  are a unique repository of species  diversity we are destroying plants and  animals and I mean individual animals we  are making species of plants and animals  extinct so that they will never live  again on earth at an appalling rate I  don't think we have a right to do that  in the first place and in the second  place there are many practical uses that  such plants and animals can have for the  human species  so it's foolish as you correctly said to  do that secondly the question has said  in places like the Philippines where he  comes from the forests remaining stands  of forests old forests are being  destroyed because poor people need the  trees for lumber for firewood and so on  and this is connected with the large  fraction of the gross national product  of such nations that goes to the  retirement of debt the questioner asks  if international debt the questioner  asks if we're all in this greenhouse  together and if the developing countries  the one  that have lent the money are the biggest  polluters on the planet might there not  be a reason for them to ease that  retirement requirements or you can say  this but maybe you meant  cancel them altogether you want my  personal opinion absolutely the the idea  of a crushing debt burden prevents  education prevents development it  prevents 